# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must keep LF endings. Checked out with CRLF on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and then run on Linux — Cloud Shell, Cloud Build,
# the container itself — they fail with "bad interpreter: ...^M", which reads as
# a broken script rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
